Examples for `gr-isdbt-gpu` live in this directory. They include GNU Radio
Companion flowgraphs, generated Python scripts and an external datacasting
example repository mounted as a Git submodule.

## Local examples

- `tx_demo.grc` / `tx_demo.py`: basic ISDB-T transmitter demo.
- `rx_demo.grc` / `rx_demo.py`: basic ISDB-T receiver demo.
- `full_transceiver.grc` / `full_transceiver_isdbt.py`: combined transceiver
  flowgraph.
- `tx_demo_13seg.grc`: 13-segment transmission demo.
- `obtaining_parameters.grc`: helper flowgraph for parameter inspection.
- `viewing_the_constellation.grc`: constellation visualization example.

## Datacasting (C++ blocks)

Ports of the TransIsdtb Python datacasting flowgraphs to the C++ blocks in
this repository (`isdbt.datacast_tx`, `isdbt.datacast_rx`, `isdbt.rms_monitor`,
`isdbt.mer_snr_estimator`, `isdbt.metrics_logger`). Requires the module to be
built and installed (`cmake --install build`).

- `datacast_tx_demo.grc`: adapted from `tx_demo.grc`, replacing the static
  `layer_a.ts` file source with `isdbt.datacast_tx` (TUN capture -> MPE
  encapsulation -> ISDB-Tb Layer A). Compiles with `grcc`.
- `datacast_rx_demo.grc`: adapted from `rx_demo.grc`, replacing the
  placeholder embedded-Python block with `isdbt.datacast_rx`, writing the
  recovered UDP payload to `/tmp/datacast_payload.bin`. Compiles with `grcc`.
- `datacast_loopback_demo.py`: minimal end-to-end test connecting
  `datacast_tx` directly to `datacast_rx` (no ISDB-Tb PHY, no RF) over TUN
  interfaces `tun0`/`tun1`. Requires root. Validates the C++ port of the
  encapsulation/carousel/reorder/rescue logic without SDR hardware.
- `metrics_demo.py`: synthetic noisy-QPSK source feeding
  `rms_monitor`/`mer_snr_estimator`/`metrics_logger`, to see the metrics
  pipeline's console/CSV output without a real receiver. Runs with no
  special privileges.

## Datacasting submodule

`TransIsdtb` is included as `examples/TransIsdtb` and contains experimental
datacasting material: SDR flowgraphs, embedded Python blocks, packet recovery
scripts, metric consolidation and plotting utilities.

Initialize it after cloning with:

```bash
git submodule update --init --recursive
```

See `../docs/datacasting-isdbtb.md` for the architecture and experimental
methodology.
